>> title: Candied Yams
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: sweet potato, brown sugar, baked, southern, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: yams, candied sweet potatoes, sweet potato souffle, sweet potato soufflé, glazed sweet potatoes
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 25 min
>> pairs-with: baked-turkey-wings, collard-greens, cornbread-dressing
>> step.1: Peel real sweet potatoes. These are not yams, whatever the shop calls them.
>> step.2: peel, cut in 1/2-in coins
>> step.3: melt to a syrup, 5 min
>> step.4: toss into the dish
>> step.5: bake 375°F 55 min, basted once

Peel real sweet potatoes for this.

Peel @sweet potatoes{3%lb}(1.4 kg) and cut them into 1/2-in coins.

Melt @unsalted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g), @light brown sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp} in a #saucepan{} and ~simmer{5%min} to a loose syrup.

Toss @&(~2)sweet potato coins{} with @&(~1)spiced syrup{} in a #baking dish{}.

Bake @&(~1)glazed sweet potatoes{} covered at 375°F (190°C) for ~bake{55%min}, basting once when the syrup starts to catch at the edges.

Mash the whole pan with a fork and put it back for twenty minutes and it is sweet potato soufflé.
